      "id": 1,
      "text": "Wisner was founded in 1892 by Edward Wisner, a Michigan native who moved south in 1888 for health reasons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wisner%2C_Louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Edward Wisner pioneered large-scale drainage, turning swamp into farmland and earning the title 'Father of Reclamation'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/wisner_louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Wisner sits near Bayou Macon and the Tensas River, waterways that historically guided early settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/wisner_louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wisner lies along U.S. Route 425, linking north to Winnsboro and south to Sicily Island.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
